-- title:
--   Fricke involution carries the level-one inclusion to q-rescaling
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number, nonzero. Write $F^{\mathrm{full}}_N \subset \mathbb{Q}((t))$ for the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by `divisorExpansions N`, and for a field $L$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ let $\overline{F}_N =$ `laurentBaseChange` $L\, F^{\mathrm{full}}_N$ be the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $F^{\mathrm{full}}_N$; here $L = \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$. Two $L$-algebra maps $\overline{F}_{1} \to \overline{F}_{1\cdot q}$ are in play: `heckeAlphaBar`, the inclusion of subfields of $L((t))$ arising from the containment $F^{\mathrm{full}}_{1} \subseteq F^{\mathrm{full}}_{1\cdot q}$ for $1 \mid 1\cdot q$, and `heckeBetaBar`, the map induced by `qExpand` $L\,q$, the ring homomorphism of $L((t))$ multiplying all exponents by $q$ (substitution $t \mapsto t^{q}$). Let `frickeInvolutionBar` $(1\cdot q)$ be the $L$-algebra automorphism of $\overline{F}_{1 \cdot q}$ obtained by base change along `geomAut` from `frickeInvolutionFull` $(1\cdot q)$, the automorphism of $F^{\mathrm{full}}_{1\cdot q}$ chosen to satisfy `IsFrickeAutFull` $(1\cdot q)$ when such an automorphism exists and the identity otherwise. The assertion is that `heckeAlphaBar` followed by `frickeInvolutionBar` $(1\cdot q)$ equals `heckeBetaBar`.
--
--   This is the level-one case $N = 1$ of the compatibility of the Fricke–Atkin–Lehner automorphism with the two degeneracy embeddings: on the field of level $1$, generated by the $j$-expansion, the Fricke involution of $X_0(q)$ carries a function to the same function with $q$-expansion variable rescaled by $q$. It feeds the study of prolongation pairs and of specialisations of places of the level-one field, in particular the lemmas on residues of the $j$-function in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization`](def/ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization.html#L13).
-- source:
